OpenKernel
==========

OpenKernel is an experimental freestanding 32-bit x86 kernel. It boots through
GRUB/Multiboot, reads a USTAR initramfs, and provides a limited syscall,
filesystem, display, and input implementation. Loaded programs currently run
at kernel privilege in shared memory; this is not a protected microkernel.

The maintained project introduction is in README.md. Full implementation
documentation is indexed at documenetation/index.md, including build and boot
instructions, syscall and program-loader references, filesystem behavior,
userspace shell, display/input, sound/time, interrupts, memory, and known
incomplete features.
